Mortar runs in a Solid 2 app built with Vite and `@solidjs/vite-plugin` 3. If you're starting from scratch, set that up first, with SSR if you want pages rendered on the server.

## Install the packages

```sh
pnpm add @mortar-kit/core @mortar-kit/admin solid-js @solidjs/web @solidjs/router
```

Add a theme if you want one, for example:

```sh
pnpm add @mortar-kit/theme-midnight
```

## Configure Vite

Add `mortarKit()` next to the Solid plugin. It only chooses the admin's theme, so leave out `theme` for the default look.

```ts
// vite.config.ts
import { mortarKit } from '@mortar-kit/admin/vite';
import midnight from '@mortar-kit/theme-midnight';
import solid from '@solidjs/vite-plugin';
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [
    solid({ start: { renderMode: 'async' }, ssr: true, serverFunctions: true }),
    mortarKit({ theme: midnight }),
  ],
});
```

## TypeScript

Use Solid 2's JSX settings:

```json
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "jsx": "preserve",
    "jsxImportSource": "@solidjs/web",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler"
  }
}
```

Next, build a first page in the [quick start](/docs/quick-start).
